{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}L1·L2·L3 · the news, and what it's evidence of{% endblock %}
{% block body_class %}archive-page{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<div class="wrap">
  <header class="masthead">
    <p class="mast-date">L1 · L2 · L3</p>
    <h1 class="mast-title">The news, and <mark>what it's evidence of.</mark></h1>
    <p class="lead">Every morning this reads about 270 headlines, explains the 25 that matter, and shows which longer
      patterns they belong to.</p>
    {% if latest %}<a class="btn" href="{{ latest.file }}">Read today's edition ({{ latest.day }}) →</a>{% endif %}
  </header>

  <section class="about" id="how">
    <h2 class="h2">How to read it</h2>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-card r1">
        <span class="rung-l">L1</span><span class="rung-t">What happened</span>
        <p>One headline, one day. Explained so you get the gist without the article.</p>
        <p class="about-eg">e.g. Nvidia backs Simplismart, a startup that cuts the cost of running AI models.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-card r2">
        <span class="rung-l">L2</span><span class="rung-t">The pattern</span>
        <p>Something many headlines are evidence of. Lasts weeks or months. This is the part worth remembering.</p>
        <p class="about-eg">e.g. Investors are shifting money from building AI models to making them cheaper to run.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-card r3">
        <span class="rung-l">L3</span><span class="rung-t">The force</span>
        <p>The deep driver behind every pattern. Always one of five: Technology, Money, Geopolitics, Rules, People.</p>
        <p class="about-eg">e.g. Money: capital goes where returns look most reliable.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>Headlines are forgotten in a day; patterns are what help you understand the next one. Each edition has
      three tabs: <b>News</b> (today's stories, explained), <b>What it means</b> (the patterns and forces), and
      <b>Play</b> (a quick quiz, including patterns from earlier days so they stick).</p>
    <p class="credit">💡 The L1 / L2 / L3 idea comes from <a href="{{ credit.url }}">{{ credit.name }}</a> on Instagram.
      This site is one person's implementation of it.</p>
  </section>

  <h2 class="h2">All editions</h2>
  <div class="archive">
    {% for e in editions %}
    <a class="tile{{ ' is-latest' if loop.first }}{{ ' is-weekly' if e.weekly }}" href="{{ e.file }}">
      <span class="tile-kind">{{ "Latest · " if loop.first }}{{ "Weekly" if e.weekly else "Daily" }}</span>
      <span class="tile-date">{{ e.day }}</span>
      <span class="tile-lead">{{ e.lead }}</span>
    </a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
